r","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbrandes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learner-dashboard/commits/a555909140e06f0e59561b11f9f11e48eff34b3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:55:32Z","email":"adolfo@axim.org","name":"Adolfo R. Brandes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:55:32Z","email":"arbrandes@arbrand.es","name":"Adolfo R. Brandes"},"message":"build: adopt the OEP-10 ADR 0002 branch layout\n\nRenames this repository''s stable line from release/frontend-base to\nstable, per openedx/public-engineering#563, and teaches semantic-release\nthe full OEP-10 ADR 0002 layout: maintenance branches first, then stable\non the latest dist-tag, then master publishing alphas.\n\nThe maintenance patterns cost nothing until a maintenance branch is\nactually cut - semantic-release skips configured branches that do not\nexist - but having them here means a new line starts publishing the\nmoment it is pushed.\n\nrelease.yml has to move in the same commit. A state where .releaserc\nnames master and stable while the workflow still triggers on\nfrontend-base would run semantic-release against a config that does not\nlist the branch it is on. While in there, the actions are pinned to\ncommit SHAs and the runner moves to ubuntu-latest, matching the rest of\nthe org.","tree":{"sha":"ad476134c2f4545bffc2bb9ffb6afcf1e2245d65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learner-dashboard/git/trees/ad476134c2f4545bffc2bb9ffb6afcf1e2245d65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learner-dashboard/git/commits/a555909140e06f0e59561b11f9f11e48eff34b3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/759355?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbrandes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbrandes/fol