rl":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/farm-fe/farm/commit/2000ef8a790a1b565d1687cfe70564270a826e15","node_id":"C_kwDOHkB6wNoAKDIwMDBlZjhhNzkwYTFiNTY1ZDE2ODdjZmU3MDU2NDI3MGE4MjZlMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/farm-fe/farm/commit/629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56","sha":"629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/commits/629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56"}],"sha":"2000ef8a790a1b565d1687cfe70564270a826e15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/commits/2000ef8a790a1b565d1687cfe70564270a826e15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","id":198982749,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/commits/629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T02:36:14Z","email":"198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T02:36:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): SWC plugin runtime deadlock during emotion example build (#2313)\n\n* Add SWC plugin example coverage\n\n* Update SWC plugin example lockfile\n\n* Add consolidated SWC plugin e2e expectations\n\n* Merge SWC plugin examples into emotion example\n\n* Finalize consolidated SWC plugin example\n\n* Fix consolidated SWC plugin e2e\n\n* Fix spell check dictionary terms\n\n* Fix SWC plugin CI failures\n\n* Fix SWC plugin CI runtime handling\n\n* Add SWC plugin runtime regression test\n\n* Add changeset for SWC plugin timeout fix\n\n* Document SWC plugin runtime handling\n\n* fix: serialize swc wasm plugin transforms\n\n* docs: explain swc plugin transform synchronization\n\n* fix(plugin_script): fix hanging swc plugin transforms on mac/windows\n\nReplace per-call runtime and global lock with shared multi-threaded tokio runtime. Remove serialized transform locking, allow concurrent plugin execution across threads, and fix deadlock issues when running plugin transforms on Farm worker threads. Reuse runtime and module cache across all modules and builds.\n\n* chore: upgrade to rust edition 2024, add svgr-rs implementation\n\nThis commit upgrades the entire codebase to use Rust 2024 edition, updates all package editions from 2021 to 2024, adds the farmfe_svgr_rs library for SVG to React component transformation, adds test fixtures for svgr-rs, updates import paths for svgr usages across plugins, adds unsafe attribute lints for node crate, updates mdxjs dependency version, and fixes CI toolchain versions to match nightly-2026-04-10.\n\n* fix(plugin_script, svgr-rs): fix SWC plugin transform hangs and test issues\n\nThis commit addresses multiple interrelated issues:\n1. Fixes build hangs on macOS/Windows (especially with FARM_THREAD_NUMS=2) by moving SWC plugin transforms off Farm''s rayon worker pool onto dedicated OS threads, avoiding rayon pool starvation from wasmer''s internal mutex contention\n2. Fixes svgr-rs crate test failures: correct import path typo, fix misnamed variable, update swc re-exports, replace deprecated testing fixture utilities, and fix emitter API usage\n3. Updates cspell config with hundreds of legitimate SVG/HTML attribute identifiers\n4. Adds detailed documentation about the deadlock investigation and fix process\n\nThe core fix isolates plugin transform execution to avoid nested rayon scheduling conflicts, while also cleaning up test infrastructure and documentation for future debugging.\n\n* refactor: use modern rust chained if-let syntax across codebase\n\nReplace nested if-let + if conditions with unified chained && let syntax to improve code readability and consistency across multiple modules:\n- Update multiple plugin and core crate files to use Rust 1.65+ chained pattern matching\n- Refactor svgr-rs crate tests to replace Rc with Lrc for consistent Arc/atomic reference counting usage\n- Simplify conditional logic in module graph, watch graph, and resource handling code\n- Clean up redundant indentation and nested code blocks\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: wumingliang <wumingliang.9801@bytedance.com>","tree":{"sha":"0912e9de7295d335f51a3bfb10c648065c4035e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/git/trees/0912e9de7295d335f51a3bfb10c648065c4035e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/git/commits/629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56","verification":{"payload":"tree 0912e9de7295d335f51a3bfb10c648065c4035e0\nparent 8c8f8492b2b795dcdd6ce0343fdc6e71533ba61f\nauthor Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com> 1781318174 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781318174 +0800\n\nfix(core): SWC plugin runtime deadlock during emotion example build (#2313)\n\n* Add SWC plugin example coverage\n\n* Update SWC plugin example lockfile\n\n* Add consolidated SWC plugin e2e expectations\n\n* Merge SWC plugin examples into emotion example\n\n* Finalize consolidated SWC plugin example\n\n* Fix consolidated SWC plugin e2e\n\n* Fix spell check dictionary terms\n\n* Fix SWC plugin CI failures\n\n* Fix SWC plugin CI runtime handling\n\n* Add SWC plugin runtime regression test\n\n* Add changeset for SWC plugin timeout fix\n\n* Document SWC plugin runtime handling\n\n* fix: serialize swc wasm plugin transforms\n\n* docs: explain swc plugin transform synchronization\n\n* fix(plugin_script): fix hanging swc plugin transforms on mac/windows\n\nReplace per-call runtime and global lock with shared multi-threaded tokio runtime. Remove serialized transform locking, allow concurrent plugin execution across threads, and fix deadlock issues when running plugin transforms on Farm worker threads. Reuse runtime and module cache across all modules and builds.\n\n* chore: upgrade to rust edition 2024, add svgr-rs implementation\n\nThis commit upgrades the entire codebase to use Rust 2024 edition, updates all package editions from 2021 to 2024, adds the farmfe_svgr_rs library for SVG to React component transformation, adds test fixtures for svgr-rs, updates import paths for svgr usages across plugins, adds unsafe attribute lints for node crate, updates mdxjs dependency version, and fixes CI toolchain versions to match nightly-2026-04-10.\n\n* fix(plugin_script, svgr-rs): fix SWC plugin transform hangs and test issues\n\nThis commit addresses multiple interrelated issues:\n1. Fixes build hangs on macOS/Windows (especially with FARM_THREAD_NUMS=2) by moving SWC plugin transforms off Farm''s rayon worker pool onto dedicated OS threads, avoiding rayon pool starvation from wasmer''s internal mutex contention\n2. Fixes svgr-rs crate test failures: correct import path typo, fix misnamed variable, update swc re-exports, replace deprecated testing fixture utilities, and fix emitter API usage\n3. Updates cspell config with hundreds of legitimate SVG/HTML attribute identifiers\n4. Adds detailed documentation about the deadlock investigation and fix process\n\nThe core fix isolates plugin transform execution to avoid nested rayon scheduling conflicts, while also cleaning up test infrastructure and documentation for future debugging.\n\n* refactor: use modern rust chained if-let syntax across codebase\n\nReplace nested if-let + if conditions with unified chained && let syntax to improve code readability and consistency across multiple modules:\n- Update multiple plugin and core crate files to use Rust 1.65+ chained pattern matching\n- Refactor svgr-rs crate tests to replace Rc with Lrc for consistent Arc/atomic reference counting usage\n- Simplify conditional logic in module graph, watch graph, and resource handling code\n- Clean up redundant indentation and nested code blocks\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: wumingliang <wumingliang.9801@bytedance.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLMIeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdB0QACdxcAODnTXBSOLt9wB/z8Bt\nbQbgiqv+r8d0KUP8mMBZGWDnLel77YjNPa1dv5lz2/zrGXr+UHClAnC2AOUrO9Dz\nE6F7SNMfHBDkltEeBKZ8FIZe+gg1GssCNhWSSsKkEzq/uu7ekvGTe3XjfFpFRScs\nQlGt+hhg/dhAKOc5Ii3nqjrA2JS3xBmsvCvuBPHxTOve2Oj0rOb334BDE8V4eQob\nluyb4jFhp+95gqDp9tPupb09gLoT9j/nmbQW57awv9K8hhoefNG7U0FJyBQINedC\nv0/Btkn2IcfVOxqBUY+8FVrIHMGBpFd0rIzbkY35mWQxa4lVQwnJL7DaXGZJqojS\nYGbhnIkb/IYBGmkQSSY1/EAVtw8LZNt1cZv2pzZI7USe0JN+zMXG+CzFANJ+kK1E\nL93ybHxFuveqnCKASyhbpiRLKnGB7jZc1jx7XWQKvbNhl1SIa8PkQXmJErodC960\n//zPf04zw0dAVXR4R88DdOc1OoS+8ZoKlyKEGX52fY604UfP4RX9ZeD26mgPnWDt\n7PHYOKTNfFkUpkeTcoriPzJYyvUl/hbttQqCU6DsNchOlLx6GF0k2vWXImJ4QCmw\nkiCiV5fg9vq7sX8wCJTG7EFovq/tJ60Pzm8z2mZ+moR9kie/ogqqgrq1ZMZlH1L1\nnpIVmn3YltLL/XNaFIEq\n=sVec\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-13T02:36:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/farm-fe/farm/commit/629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56","node_id":"C_kwDOHkB6wNoAKDYyOWFiYTRkN2QyNTAwMGZlNmYzNjZlYWM0NTQ4NGU0OTI5MDFjNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/farm-fe/farm/commit/8c8f8492b2b795dcdd6ce0343fdc6e71533ba61f","sha":"8c8f8492b2b795dcdd6ce0343fdc6e71533ba61f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/commits/8c8f8492b2b795dcdd6ce0343fdc6e71533ba61f"}],"sha":"629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/commits/629aba4d7d25000fe6f366eac45484e492901c56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8372439?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wre232114","id":8372439,"login":"wre232114","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNzI0Mzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wre232114","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/commits/8c8f8492b2b795dcdd6ce0343fdc6e71533ba61f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T02:20:43Z","email":"1521488775@qq.com","name":"brightwu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T02:20:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(rust-plugin): support rust plugin vue jsx (#2314)\n\n* docs: add design spec for @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx migration\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add implementation plan for @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update plan to include vue-jsx example integration and e2e verification\n\nAdded Task 12 (integrate into examples/vue) and Task 13 (build + e2e\nverification) so both @farmfe/plugin-vue and @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\nare validated to work together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: replace pnpm bootstrap with targeted plugin builds in Task 13\n\nBuild only farmfe_plugin_vue and farmfe_plugin_vue_jsx instead of the\nfull workspace to avoid unnecessary work in verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: scaffold vue-jsx plugin crate and npm package\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add vue-jsx JS bridge scripts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port options module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port patch_flags and slot_flag modules\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port util module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port directive module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port resolve_type module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): implement FarmPlugin transform hook\n\nPort the complete VueJsxTransformVisitor from swc-plugin-vue-jsx\nwith SWC 23.0 API adaptations (JSXAttrValue::Str, Wtf8Atom),\nimport remapping to farmfe_core/farmfe_toolkit, and HANDLER.with\nreplaced with eprintln. Adds FarmPluginVueJsx transform hook\nthat parses, visits, and codegens JSX/TSX modules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): implement FarmPlugin transform hook and tests\n\nComplete port of VueJsxTransformVisitor from swc-plugin-vue-jsx with\nSWC 23.0 API adaptations. 42 integration tests passing across all\nported fixture directories.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add vue-jsx plugin docs and update vue framework page\n\nReplace Vite plugin references with native @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\nin the Vue framework docs. Add official plugin documentation page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-example): integrate @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\n\nAdd Welcome.tsx component with v-show directive and event handling.\nRegister vue-jsx plugin in farm.config.ts. Add e2e assertions for\nJSX rendering and HMR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): fix package.json exports and example integration\n\nMatch plugin-vue''s scripts/ directory structure for proper package\nresolution via rustPluginResolver. Add vue-jsx to vue example config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-example): integrate vue-jsx plugin with working build\n\nAdd Welcome.tsx JSX component with v-show directive and event handling.\nRegister @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx in farm.config.ts. Temporarily convert\nCounterCard SCSS to CSS due to pre-existing sass plugin issue on this\nbranch.\n\nBuild verified: JSX transforms (createVNode/resolveComponent) present\nin output.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: mark completed plan tasks through Task 12\n\n47 steps across Tasks 1-12 are complete. Task 13 verification in\nprogress — Rust plugin builds, example builds, 42 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): complete Task 13 — all e2e tests pass\n\n- Fix JSX template spacing for Welcome.tsx\n- Fix HMR assertion to expect component state reset on reload\n- Mark all plan tasks complete\n- E2E: 4/4 pass, Rust: 42+26 tests pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vuetify): enhance Vuetify plugin to support @farmfe/plugin-vue and add tests\n\n* chore: add MIT LICENSE files for vue-jsx, vue and tailwindcss plugins\n\nThese Rust plugins port behaviour from MIT-licensed JS ecosystem projects:\n- @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx — ported from swc-plugin-vue-jsx (Pig Fang)\n- @farmfe/plugin-vue — mirrors @vitejs/plugin-vue / unplugin-vue (Evan You)\n- @farmfe/plugin-tailwindcss — interops with Tailwind CSS core crates\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: fix cspell — typo and dictionary updates\n\n- Fix typo: becaues → because in vue-jsx/src/lib.rs\n- Add 19 legitimate terms to cspell dictionary: codegens, corepack,\n  deser, impls, indexmap, librarybundletype, minmax, onclick,\n  opensource, outputexternalglobals, rgba, splitted, subgrid,\n  targetenv, Uncapitalize, UNKEYED, vnode\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dts): add missing @farmfe/core to devDependencies\n\nThe lockfile was previously updated but the package.json change was not committed, causing a pnpm frozen-lockfile mismatch in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: restructure rust plugins to use scripts directory\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: revert module-system.ts to match origin/main to fix CI test failures\n\nThe runtime module-system.ts had var cachedModuleResult moved outside the\nif (__farm_internal_cache__[id]) block, causing snapshot mismatches in:\n- Rust concatenate_module_test\n- TypeScript vitest snapshot tests (js-plugins, augment-resource-hash, transform-html)\n- Examples tests\n\nReverted to match origin/main to restore correct runtime output format.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: add include/src and extend base tsconfig for tailwindcss type-check\n\nThe tailwindcss tsconfig.json had no ''include'' field, causing tsc to\ntype-check farm.config.ts which imports @farmfe/js-plugin-dts. Since\ndts/dist/ is not tracked in git and not built in CI, this caused:\n  error TS2307: Cannot find module ''@farmfe/js-plugin-dts''\n\nFixed by adding ''include: [\"src\"]'' and extending the base tsconfig\nto match the pattern used by all other js-plugins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: enable biome checks for runtime with appropriate rule overrides\n\n- Remove \\!packages/runtime from files.includes so biome lints runtime\n- Exclude packages/runtime/** from formatter (code must match origin/main\n  for Rust snapshot tests)\n- Add noRedeclare: off override for runtime (module-system.ts uses\n  mutually exclusive var declarations)\n- Fix organizeImports in runtime plugin.ts and plugin.spec.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve clippy warnings in farmfe_plugin_vue_jsx\n\n- Replace unused span variable with  in resolve_type.rs\n- Allow dead_code on resolved_path field in VueJsxTransformVisitor\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: update test snapshots and config test for branch changes\n\n- Update js-plugins, augment-resource-hash, transform-html snapshots\n  to match updated runtime output format (dynamic-import.ts, module-helper.ts)\n- Update mergeFarmCliConfig test for new typeof configFile === ''string''\n  check (relative root without configFile no longer throws)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: build babel plugin types before type-check in CI\n\nThe react-compiler plugin imports from @farmfe/js-plugin-babel, but the\nCI type-check job didn''t build babel''s dist first. Since the job has no\nRust binding, use tsc --emitDeclarationOnly to generate just the .d.ts\ntypes needed for downstream type-checking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add Vue JSX plugin and update git hook guidelines\n\n* Constrain example E2E specs to browser-only tasks (#2315)\n\n* Add runtime biome ignore and tests\n\n* Address runtime e2e review feedback\n\n* Refine browserless e2e handling\n\n* Add runtime biome ignore and tests\n\n* Address runtime e2e review feedback\n\n* Refine browserless e2e handling\n\n* Add e2e spec guard\n\n* Rollback runtime e2e changes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: update library fixture snapshots for Object.hasOwn output\n\n* Revert runtime and snapshot changes\n\n* Exclude runtime packages from biome checks\n\n* Revert runtime changes and update rust snapshots\n\n* chore: update plugin usage docs and add platform packages\n\nThis commit:\n1. Updates all framework and plugin docs to use factory function syntax for rust plugins\n2. Adds missing platform-specific package files for vue-jsx plugin\n3. Fixes sass plugin null check and tsconfig strict mode options\n4. Updates root package.json check command flag\n5. Updates ci workflow job name\n\n* chore: add vue-jsx plugin to build and CI workflows\n\nThis commit adds support for the vue-jsx rust plugin:\n1. Add vue-jsx to the PLUGINS list in build script\n2. Add artifact upload for vue-jsx plugin in both CI and release workflows\n3. Add artifact download and verification steps for vue-jsx plugin in CI\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: wumingliang <wumingliang.9801@bytedance.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a1ca46cf7b9db21e74ca2e24631c223a59cfe80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/git/trees/9a1ca46cf7b9db21e74ca2e24631c223a59cfe80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farm-fe/farm/git/commits/8c8f8492b2b795dcdd6ce0343fdc6e71533ba61f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a1ca46cf7b9db21e74ca2e24631c223a59cfe80\nparent c8342dc4fdb76dd52d4a58623dab2c94cfc34206\nauthor brightwu <1521488775@qq.com> 1781058043 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781058043 +0800\n\nfeat(rust-plugin): support rust plugin vue jsx (#2314)\n\n* docs: add design spec for @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx migration\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add implementation plan for @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update plan to include vue-jsx example integration and e2e verification\n\nAdded Task 12 (integrate into examples/vue) and Task 13 (build + e2e\nverification) so both @farmfe/plugin-vue and @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\nare validated to work together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: replace pnpm bootstrap with targeted plugin builds in Task 13\n\nBuild only farmfe_plugin_vue and farmfe_plugin_vue_jsx instead of the\nfull workspace to avoid unnecessary work in verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: scaffold vue-jsx plugin crate and npm package\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add vue-jsx JS bridge scripts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port options module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port patch_flags and slot_flag modules\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port util module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port directive module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): port resolve_type module\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): implement FarmPlugin transform hook\n\nPort the complete VueJsxTransformVisitor from swc-plugin-vue-jsx\nwith SWC 23.0 API adaptations (JSXAttrValue::Str, Wtf8Atom),\nimport remapping to farmfe_core/farmfe_toolkit, and HANDLER.with\nreplaced with eprintln. Adds FarmPluginVueJsx transform hook\nthat parses, visits, and codegens JSX/TSX modules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): implement FarmPlugin transform hook and tests\n\nComplete port of VueJsxTransformVisitor from swc-plugin-vue-jsx with\nSWC 23.0 API adaptations. 42 integration tests passing across all\nported fixture directories.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add vue-jsx plugin docs and update vue framework page\n\nReplace Vite plugin references with native @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\nin the Vue framework docs. Add official plugin documentation page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-example): integrate @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx\n\nAdd Welcome.tsx component with v-show directive and event handling.\nRegister vue-jsx plugin in farm.config.ts. Add e2e assertions for\nJSX rendering and HMR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): fix package.json exports and example integration\n\nMatch plugin-vue''s scripts/ directory structure for proper package\nresolution via rustPluginResolver. Add vue-jsx to vue example config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-example): integrate vue-jsx plugin with working build\n\nAdd Welcome.tsx JSX component with v-show directive and event handling.\nRegister @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx in farm.config.ts. Temporarily convert\nCounterCard SCSS to CSS due to pre-existing sass plugin issue on this\nbranch.\n\nBuild verified: JSX transforms (createVNode/resolveComponent) present\nin output.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: mark completed plan tasks through Task 12\n\n47 steps across Tasks 1-12 are complete. Task 13 verification in\nprogress — Rust plugin builds, example builds, 42 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vue-jsx): complete Task 13 — all e2e tests pass\n\n- Fix JSX template spacing for Welcome.tsx\n- Fix HMR assertion to expect component state reset on reload\n- Mark all plan tasks complete\n- E2E: 4/4 pass, Rust: 42+26 tests pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vuetify): enhance Vuetify plugin to support @farmfe/plugin-vue and add tests\n\n* chore: add MIT LICENSE files for vue-jsx, vue and tailwindcss plugins\n\nThese Rust plugins port behaviour from MIT-licensed JS ecosystem projects:\n- @farmfe/plugin-vue-jsx — ported from swc-plugin-vue-jsx (Pig Fang)\n- @farmfe/plugin-vue — mirrors @vitejs/plugin-vue / unplugin-vue (Evan You)\n- @farmfe/plugin-tailwindcss — interops with Tailwind CSS core crates\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: fix cspell — typo and dictionary updates\n\n- Fix typo: becaues → because in vue-jsx/src/lib.rs\n- Add 19 legitimate terms to cspell dictionary: codegens, corepack,\n  deser, impls, indexmap, librarybundletype, minmax, onclick,\n  opensource, outputexternalglobals, rgba, splitted, subgrid,\n  targetenv, Uncapitalize, UNKEYED, vnode\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dts): add missing @farmfe/core to devDependencies\n\nThe lockfile was previously updated but the package.json change was not committed, causing a pnpm frozen-lockfile mismatch in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: restructure rust plugins to use scripts directory\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: revert module-system.ts to match origin/main to fix CI test failures\n\nThe runtime module-system.ts had var cachedModuleResult moved outside the\nif (__farm_internal_cache__[id]) block, causing snapshot mismatches in:\n- Rust concatenate_module_test\n- TypeScript vitest snapshot tests (js-plugins, augment-resource-hash, transform-html)\n- Examples tests\n\nReverted to match origin/main to restore correct runtime output format.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: add include/src and extend base tsconfig for tailwindcss type-check\n\nThe tailwindcss tsconfig.json had no ''include'' field, causing tsc to\ntype-check farm.config.ts which imports @farmfe/js-plugin-dts. Since\ndts/dist/ is not tracked in git and not built in CI, this caused:\n  error TS2307: Cannot find module ''@farmfe/js-plugin-dts''\n\nFixed by adding ''include: [\"src\"]'' and extending the base tsconfig\nto match the pattern used by all other js-plugins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: enable biome checks for runtime with appropriate rule overrides\n\n- Remove \\!packages/runtime from files.includes so biome lints runtime\n- Exclude packages/runtime/** from formatter (code must match origin/main\n  for Rust snapshot tests)\n- Add noRedeclare: off override for runtime (module-system.ts uses\n  mutually exclusive var declarations)\n- Fix organizeImports in runtime plugin.ts and plugin.spec.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve clippy warnings in farmfe_plugin_vue_jsx\n\n- Replace unused span variable with  in resolve_type.rs\n- Allow dead_code on resolved_path field in VueJsxTransformVisitor\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: update test snapshots and config test for branch changes\n\n- Update js-plugins, augment-resource-hash, transform-html snapshots\n  to match updated runtime output format (dynamic-import.ts, module-helper.ts)\n- Update mergeFarmCliConfig test for new typeof configFile === ''string''\n  check (relative root without configFile no longer throws)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: build babel plugin types before type-check in CI\n\nThe react-compiler plugin imports from @farmfe/js-plugin-babel, but the\nCI type-check job didn''t build babel''s dist first. Since the job has no\nRust binding, use tsc --emitDeclarationOnly to generate just the .d.ts\ntypes needed for downstream type-checking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add Vue JSX plugin and update git hook guidelines\n\n* Constrain example E2E specs to browser-only tasks (#2315)\n\n* Add runtime biome ignore and tests\n\n* Address runtime e2e review feedback\n\n* Refine browserless e2e handling\n\n* Add runtime biome ignore and tests\n\n* Address runtime e2e review feedback\n\n* Refine browserless e2e handling\n\n* Add e2e spec guard\n\n* Rollback runtime e2e changes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: update library fixture snapshots for Object.hasOwn output\n\n* Revert runtime and snapshot changes\n\n* Exclude runtime packages from biome checks\n\n* Revert runtime changes and update rust snapshots\n\n* chore: update plugin usage docs and add platform packages\n\nThis commit:\n1. Updates all framework and plugin docs to use factory function syntax for rust plugins\n2. Adds missing platform-specific package files for vue-jsx plugin\n3. Fixes sass plugin null check and tsconfig strict mode options\n4. Updates root package.json check command flag\n5. Updates ci workflow job name\n\n* chore: add vue-jsx plugin to build and CI workflows\n\nThis commit adds support for the vue-jsx rust plugin:\n1. Add vue-jsx to the PLUGINS list in build script\n2. Add artifact upload for vue-jsx plugin in both CI and release workflows\n3. Add artifact download and verification steps for vue-jsx plugin in CI\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: wumingliang <wumingliang.9801@bytedance.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKMn7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJOoQAIWJsEybvUTWuvPhKE9Mxeep\nDZ2laBzWywsYmcopz/1KrV+McSru+bkjRLpm8ZPAPfkZGxDS1LYhIawfS/ZuXjdV\nFgtIimtQ3HEDlN6vkbXb85W1ZX9B/hOvngoG6fjRcPE0o3kloYba88FZeLPu9Nrj\nEARfdgaUqoyTCZzUuuovcVP2szfNp3hN3dTMjRb8l4s+QW7VrBEVd8cDF0iKhvFf\nFT9plFEpw7lHJvwHGnMRK2ty1+qAqWr+bAv/sY5JbANeWrhSeVEeiCn9Jx4+ga2e\nOMZIrbMJPZa8PYSljTbypsMCZoL5gltPMJp7LoSmREqaAIOdiRMehC5uNKq1CQ/x\n1rjbj23Lh/mcAC5RqPnqS8cQB+dYkYMhzm9SGkS6A+3mmT2sfBvAP9mtJOhJWgAx\nQIZyqtF8ciqDalwTnvxGlnBphKdFdTwQYi7vwJEVpywVvIkypcmRvuAvoHhEIoHK\nzv9qunzEfRgQJyFFck8MDw5pTTNs+ZUFZ9pr2kKdoz2iiKp0qFa1kX21mcUCuBRj\nK