de generation.\n- Updated `generate_dts` function in both `generate_dts.rs` files to utilize the new struct for improved readability and maintainability.\n\nEnhance compression plugin for parallel processing\n\n- Modified the compression plugin to use a channel for handling results from parallel compression tasks.\n- Replaced the use of `par_iter` with `iter_mut` to allow mutable access to resources during compression.\n- Improved error handling for result collection from parallel tasks.\n\nClean up WASM plugin by removing unused cache functionality\n\n- Removed the `CachedStaticAssets` struct and related caching logic from the WASM plugin.\n- Simplified the plugin implementation by focusing on the core functionality without caching overhead.\n\nUpdate build scripts to support specific example builds\n\n- Enhanced the `buildExamples` function to accept an optional `example` parameter for targeted builds.\n- Added argument parsing for the `--example` flag in the test examples script to facilitate example-specific testing.\n\nCo-authored-by: wre232114 <8372439+wre232114@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(worker): enhance worker functionality and inline support\n\n- Added new CSS styles for displaying worker cases and their statuses.\n- Updated the Main component to accept worker results and display them.\n- Refactored the worker implementation to expose a simpler API using Comlink.\n- Introduced a new shared worker implementation to handle messages.\n- Removed the old cache implementation and replaced it with a new code generation module.\n- Implemented worker URL computation and entry name generation for better output management.\n- Enhanced the plugin to handle inline workers and dynamic entries more effectively.\n- Added resource patching to replace inline worker placeholders with actual base64-encoded content.\n- Introduced options struct for better configuration management.\n\nCo-authored-by: wre232114 <8372439+wre232114@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: add 